1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:01,533
<i>Andrew, Dad's body isn't there.</i>

2
00:00:01,667 --> 00:00:02,733
<i> They have nothing to show.</i>

3
00:00:02,867 --> 00:00:04,433
<i> Maybe it's in another room.</i>

4
00:00:04,567 --> 00:00:06,067
<i>If you don't want to believe it,
then don't.</i>

5
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,667
<i>If only I knew where he went...</i>

6
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,767
<i>I heard Major was given a
mission order</i>

7
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:13,300
<i> for a mission in the North.</i>

8
00:00:13,433 --> 00:00:15,300
<i>If there's one person who knows</i>

9
00:00:15,433 --> 00:00:16,567
<i> where he went,</i>

10
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:17,600
<i> it's Lansang.</i>

11
00:00:17,733 --> 00:00:19,000
<i> Ah, can I talk to you</i>

12
00:00:19,133 --> 00:00:21,667
<i> about Major Delgado's case?</i>

13
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:23,567
<i>Dad was sent to the town of
Valmora,</i>

14
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:26,000
<i>and Berdugo is supposed
to take over</i>

15
00:00:26,133 --> 00:00:28,433
<i>drug operations
in the North there.</i>

16
00:00:28,567 --> 00:00:30,567
<i> We need a lot of product</i>

17
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:32,033
<i> for the new stronghold.</i>

18
00:00:32,167 --> 00:00:34,000
<i>You and Delilah have really gone
your separate ways.</i>

19
00:00:34,167 --> 00:00:35,667
<i> He needs us now, Jin Ho.</i>

20
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,200
<i>Just tell me about
Joey's father.</i>

21
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:37,900
<i> What happened? What happened?</i>

22
00:00:38,033 --> 00:00:38,967
<i> I strongly feel</i>

23
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:41,300
<i>it was a syndicate
that went after him.</i>

24
00:00:41,433 --> 00:00:42,800
<i> I feel bad for Joey.</i>

25
00:00:42,933 --> 00:00:45,800
<i>If what you're saying is true
that he's alive...</i>

26
00:00:45,933 --> 00:00:47,700
<i>then he should already be here.</i>

27
00:00:47,833 --> 00:00:50,000
<i>Joey is still in denial
about her father's death.</i>

28
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,633
<i> She's been through a lot.</i>

29
00:00:51,767 --> 00:00:54,800
<i> But her plan to go North</i>

30
00:00:54,933 --> 00:00:56,733
<i>thinking she'll still
find her father...</i>

31
00:00:56,867 --> 00:00:58,033
<i> I can't let her do that alone.</i>

32
00:00:58,167 --> 00:01:00,400
<i>Major Delgado
entrusted her to me.</i>

33
00:01:00,533 --> 00:01:01,833
<i> Andrew Dizon talked to me.</i>

34
00:01:01,967 --> 00:01:04,300
<i>He's been pushing
for DNA confirmation.</i>

35
00:01:04,433 --> 00:01:06,133
<i>You already know
what to tell him, right?</i>

36
00:01:06,267 --> 00:01:08,000
<i>How long are we going
to hide this?</i>

37
00:01:08,167 --> 00:01:09,500
<i> I'm starting to believe</i>

38
00:01:09,633 --> 00:01:11,233
<i>that maybe your father
really is alive.</i>

39
00:01:11,367 --> 00:01:13,100
<i>That they're not telling you
everything.</i>

40
00:01:13,233 --> 00:01:15,833
<i> We'll find your father.</i>

41
00:01:43,967 --> 00:01:44,833
Joey...

42
00:01:44,967 --> 00:01:46,167
Mom?

43
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:50,500
Can't you just...

44
00:01:50,633 --> 00:01:54,633
do your school work online?

45
00:01:55,433 --> 00:01:56,933
I really need

46
00:01:57,067 --> 00:01:59,000
to be there in person, Mom.

47
00:01:59,133 --> 00:02:00,867
We haven't even gotten
your father back yet,

48
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,633
and now you're leaving.

49
00:02:03,633 --> 00:02:05,667
Mom, I'll come back right away.

50
00:02:06,567 --> 00:02:08,400
I just really need to do this

51
00:02:08,533 --> 00:02:10,100
in person.

52
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:13,133
Maybe you need...

53
00:02:13,733 --> 00:02:15,333
a little time.

54
00:02:17,533 --> 00:02:19,800
It might even be good for you

55
00:02:19,933 --> 00:02:22,267
to get away,
even just for a while.

56
00:02:25,433 --> 00:02:26,667
But, Joey...

57
00:02:27,367 --> 00:02:30,933
I hope you're not upset with me
about what I said last night.

58
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:34,333
Mom, I'm not.
Please don't say that.

59
00:02:40,133 --> 00:02:41,867
Take care.

60
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:45,000
You too, Mom.

61
00:02:58,933 --> 00:03:00,533
Love you, Mom.

62
00:03:00,667 --> 00:03:02,433
Love you too, Joey.

63
00:03:38,167 --> 00:03:40,567
Joey, let's go?

64
00:03:41,967 --> 00:03:43,333
Let's go.

65
00:03:54,467 --> 00:03:55,567
Oh...

66
00:03:56,267 --> 00:03:58,533
you seem different today.

67
00:03:59,167 --> 00:04:00,233
Huh?

68
00:04:01,667 --> 00:04:03,333
It's nothing.

69
00:04:03,467 --> 00:04:04,767
I just fixed my hair.

70
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:06,933
Ah...

71
00:04:07,333 --> 00:04:08,767
okay.

72
00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:12,100
Hey, thanks, Andrew.

73
00:04:12,933 --> 00:04:15,100
For what?

74
00:04:16,067 --> 00:04:18,533
You really want to hear
the whole thing?

75
00:04:18,933 --> 00:04:20,533
What, you want it sweeter
or something?

76
00:04:20,667 --> 00:04:21,400
Mmm-hmm.

77
00:04:21,533 --> 00:04:23,100
Thank you, Boss Idol,

78
00:04:23,233 --> 00:04:26,467
for helping me find my father.

79
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:27,900
Is that enough?
Is that okay for you?

80
00:04:28,067 --> 00:04:30,367
Mmm...

81
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:32,100
That'll do.

82
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:34,600
You might think...

83
00:04:34,733 --> 00:04:36,733
I'm doing this just for you.

84
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:39,933
But I'm really doing this
because,

85
00:04:40,067 --> 00:04:42,133
of course, I want to be

86
00:04:42,267 --> 00:04:45,300
the first to release the exposé.

87
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:50,100
Joey...

88
00:04:51,333 --> 00:04:52,867
You have to be ready.

89
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:55,867
Because if Major is there,

90
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,033
there's a probability
we'll encounter

91
00:04:58,167 --> 00:05:01,167
the syndicates
he's dealing with,

92
00:05:01,333 --> 00:05:03,333
including Berdugo.

93
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:10,000
If this is what we need
to do for Dad,

94
00:05:11,333 --> 00:05:13,167
I'm ready, I can handle it.

95
00:05:17,167 --> 00:05:18,667
Okay.

96
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:20,600
Let's go.

97
00:05:47,367 --> 00:05:49,967
So you really did get a haircut,
huh?

98
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:53,567
Why? You didn't believe me
earlier?

99
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:54,833
Well...

100
00:05:56,433 --> 00:05:58,467
you look a bit more handsome.

101
00:06:01,067 --> 00:06:04,433
Well, you know, maybe
you should drink some water.

102
00:06:09,733 --> 00:06:11,467
I was about to open it.
I'll do it.

103
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:14,600
Wow, how nice of you.

104
00:06:14,733 --> 00:06:16,500
And at least you got more
handsome, right?

105
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:18,767
And kind, too.

106
00:06:20,533 --> 00:06:22,067
You're really feeling yourself.

107
00:06:23,700 --> 00:06:25,200
Well, anyway...

108
00:06:25,667 --> 00:06:27,900
What did you tell Ms. Clarissa?

109
00:06:28,967 --> 00:06:31,133
Honestly, I lied to her.

110
00:06:31,267 --> 00:06:33,367
I said I just had something
to do at school.

111
00:06:35,433 --> 00:06:38,167
Because you know
she wouldn't allow it

112
00:06:38,300 --> 00:06:40,167
if you told her your plan?

113
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:42,333
Well, I'm just thinking

114
00:06:42,467 --> 00:06:44,400
that maybe if I come home
with Dad,

115
00:06:44,533 --> 00:06:46,133
she'll understand.

116
00:06:47,033 --> 00:06:48,833
It's just, I don't know
where to start

117
00:06:48,967 --> 00:06:51,100
once we get to Valmora.

118
00:06:51,233 --> 00:06:53,267
I don't know the place,

119
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:56,500
and Peter and Jin Ho
aren't there to help.

120
00:06:58,400 --> 00:06:59,733
I've got it covered.

121
00:07:00,900 --> 00:07:02,800
I know someone in Valmora.

122
00:07:04,267 --> 00:07:05,967
They can help us.

123
00:07:06,833 --> 00:07:08,300
Who?

124
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:11,200
<i>I'm not just going there
for Joey.</i>

125
00:07:11,333 --> 00:07:12,900
<i> It's also for Tirada.</i>

126
00:07:13,033 --> 00:07:14,967
<i> I'm going to investigate.</i>

127
00:07:15,467 --> 00:07:18,000
<i>I want to be the first to break
the news</i>

128
00:07:18,133 --> 00:07:20,000
<i> about Berdugo's real identity.</i>

129
00:07:20,133 --> 00:07:21,767
<i> Wait.</i>

130
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:23,967
<i> Isn't that also where...</i>

131
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:25,633
<i> I have to go, I have to go.</i>

132
00:07:25,767 --> 00:07:27,200
<i> I need to prepare.</i>

133
00:07:29,267 --> 00:07:30,633
Just.

134
00:07:32,700 --> 00:07:34,100
Come on.

135
00:07:35,567 --> 00:07:36,933
Okay.

136
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:06,100
Stubborn girl.

137
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:11,900
Good morning!

138
00:08:13,033 --> 00:08:14,400
You're awake.

139
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:20,733
Are we here already?
That was fast.

140
00:08:21,967 --> 00:08:25,000
Well, that's what happens
when you sleep the whole day.

141
00:08:31,767 --> 00:08:34,300
It's so beautiful,
it looks like a painting!

142
00:08:36,067 --> 00:08:37,633
They say when you're greeted

143
00:08:37,767 --> 00:08:39,800
by a bright sky like this,

144
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:43,633
a beautiful surprise...

145
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:45,667
is waiting for you.

146
00:08:46,467 --> 00:08:48,867
I hope my surprise is Dad.

147
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:09,267
Joey, stay here for a bit.

148
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,800
Why? Where are you going?

149
00:09:12,233 --> 00:09:14,900
I just need to talk to someone
I know here.

150
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:17,467
Wait, I'll come with you.

151
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:18,533
No, no, Joey.

152
00:09:18,667 --> 00:09:20,600
I need to make sure first

153
00:09:20,733 --> 00:09:23,300
if they'll really help us.

154
00:09:24,433 --> 00:09:26,067
Stay here.

155
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:28,700
Huh?

156
00:10:31,100 --> 00:10:32,500
Zoey...

157
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:40,567
Andrew...

158
00:10:56,733 --> 00:10:58,233
Zoey...

159
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:06,167
Mmm...

160
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,833
Ah, you know what?

161
00:11:11,967 --> 00:11:14,333
I'm actually shocked
that you called me.

162
00:11:15,233 --> 00:11:18,600
So, what brings you here,
Andrew Dizon?

163
00:11:19,967 --> 00:11:21,667
I'll swallow my pride.

164
00:11:23,033 --> 00:11:24,800
I need your help.

165
00:11:26,067 --> 00:11:27,467
Help?

166
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:30,067
Well, that's a first.

167
00:11:49,767 --> 00:11:51,300
Dad?

168
00:11:58,567 --> 00:12:00,033
Dad!

169
00:12:00,767 --> 00:12:02,267
Dad, wait!

170
00:12:14,133 --> 00:12:15,567
Dad!

171
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:19,967
Dad!

172
00:12:22,333 --> 00:12:24,233
Dad, where are you?

173
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:26,833
Dad!

174
00:12:26,967 --> 00:12:27,933
Damn it...

175
00:12:28,067 --> 00:12:29,633
What's all that noise?

176
00:12:29,767 --> 00:12:31,633
Why are you yelling like that,
huh?

177
00:12:32,233 --> 00:12:34,133
You're disturbing us!

178
00:12:34,267 --> 00:12:36,300
We thought you were a cop.

179
00:12:36,433 --> 00:12:37,967
Hey, don't scold her.

180
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:40,067
Looks like Miss Beautiful here
got lost.

181
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,833
Miss Beautiful, what seems to be
the problem?

182
00:12:41,967 --> 00:12:42,967
I'm just looking for someone.

183
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:44,067
They came this way.

184
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,267
Here?

185
00:12:45,400 --> 00:12:47,967
No one gets in here
without passing thru us.

186
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:18,433
Ma'am, did you see

187
00:13:18,567 --> 00:13:20,833
the woman who was
with me earlier?

188
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,833
It looks like she left...

189
00:13:22,967 --> 00:13:25,000
she went that way.

190
00:13:25,367 --> 00:13:26,967
That way.

191
00:13:28,067 --> 00:13:29,167
This is our territory.

192
00:13:29,300 --> 00:13:30,367
Do you want us to help you?

193
00:13:30,500 --> 00:13:32,167
Come on, let's talk inside.

194
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:33,267
- Let go of me!
- Ouch!

195
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:35,200
- Go after her!
- Get over here!

196
00:13:43,567 --> 00:13:45,533
So Miss Beautiful knows
how to fight, huh.

197
00:13:45,667 --> 00:13:47,300
I like that, you've got spirit.

198
00:13:54,967 --> 00:13:56,967
Ouch! Ouch!

199
00:14:04,567 --> 00:14:06,233
Hey, stop!

200
00:14:28,867 --> 00:14:29,767
Hello, Andrew?

201
00:14:29,900 --> 00:14:30,933
Joey?

202
00:14:31,067 --> 00:14:32,600
Andrew, come here now.
I have too many enemies.

203
00:14:32,733 --> 00:14:34,200
I can't handle them alone.

204
00:14:34,333 --> 00:14:35,467
Wait, wait.

205
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:36,800
What enemies?
Where are you?

206
00:14:36,933 --> 00:14:38,433
I went into an alley,

207
00:14:38,567 --> 00:14:41,400
and there's like
a chicken farm here.

208
00:14:42,167 --> 00:14:44,933
Hurry, come here.
It's just near the eatery.

209
00:14:45,067 --> 00:14:46,800
All right, I'm coming.
I'll find it, okay?

210
00:14:46,933 --> 00:14:48,900
Hide for now.

211
00:14:49,033 --> 00:14:50,600
- Okay, all right.
- Miss beautiful!

212
00:14:50,733 --> 00:14:52,100
Come out now!

213
00:14:52,233 --> 00:14:54,000
Show yourself!

214
00:15:08,733 --> 00:15:09,933
Miss Beautiful!

215
00:15:10,067 --> 00:15:12,633
Come out now!

216
00:15:17,300 --> 00:15:18,667
Miss Beautiful!

217
00:15:22,433 --> 00:15:23,933
Come out now.

218
00:15:24,733 --> 00:15:26,733
We know that you're there.

219
00:15:27,333 --> 00:15:29,867
You don't have anywhere else
to escape anyway.

220
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:32,200
Got you!

221
00:15:34,333 --> 00:15:35,600
Stay right there!

222
00:16:02,933 --> 00:16:04,267
Where are you going?

223
00:16:05,300 --> 00:16:07,167
Your luck's running out!

224
00:16:42,100 --> 00:16:43,533
Police! Let's go!

225
00:16:58,833 --> 00:17:00,667
I'm here.
I'm sorry.

226
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:06,800
Are you hurt?

227
00:17:06,933 --> 00:17:08,500
Are you okay?

228
00:17:13,867 --> 00:17:16,100
I almost got stabbed.
Good thing you came.

229
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:18,900
Thank you.

230
00:17:26,433 --> 00:17:27,967
Thank you too.

231
00:17:32,667 --> 00:17:35,167
Joey, this is Zoey.

232
00:17:36,367 --> 00:17:37,900
Zoey, Joey.

233
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:44,233
So...

234
00:17:45,833 --> 00:17:47,433
you're Joey.

235
00:17:48,900 --> 00:17:50,667
<i> What kind of help do you need?</i>

236
00:17:51,633 --> 00:17:53,133
<i> Would it be okay if...</i>

237
00:17:53,733 --> 00:17:56,433
<i>I tell you once we're all
together with Joey?</i>

238
00:17:56,933 --> 00:17:58,233
<i> Joey?</i>

239
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,667
<i> My friend.</i>

240
00:18:02,333 --> 00:18:04,467
<i>Actually, we should
get going now</i>

241
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:06,067
<i> if that's okay with you.</i>

242
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:07,800
<i> She's waiting.</i>

243
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:10,733
So you're a woman.

244
00:18:12,533 --> 00:18:14,400
Yes, is that a problem?

245
00:18:16,167 --> 00:18:19,667
Well, from the way Andrew
told the story,

246
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:23,800
I thought the Joey
he was talking about was a guy.

247
00:18:24,933 --> 00:18:28,067
And is it a problem
if his friend is a woman?

248
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:29,167
It depends.

249
00:18:29,300 --> 00:18:30,867
How close are you as friends?

250
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,233
Ah...

251
00:18:33,667 --> 00:18:35,533
Joey, Zoey is the one
who'll help us

252
00:18:35,667 --> 00:18:37,933
while we're here in Valmora.

253
00:18:38,833 --> 00:18:40,900
She is with DDE.

254
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:45,800
That's really
your only intro for me?

255
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:48,300
What about our history?

256
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:55,667
I'm his ex-girlfriend
by the way.

257
00:18:55,833 --> 00:18:57,667
We dated for 4 years actually.

258
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:03,800
Okay.

259
00:19:12,367 --> 00:19:13,600
Joey...

260
00:19:15,933 --> 00:19:17,367
You're wounded.

261
00:19:18,100 --> 00:19:22,900
That needs to be treated.

262
00:19:39,367 --> 00:19:41,000
Hey, Peter.

263
00:19:41,133 --> 00:19:42,300
What's that?

264
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:47,167
Take a look.

265
00:19:47,300 --> 00:19:49,300
Don't tell me you're giving me
a makeover.

266
00:19:49,433 --> 00:19:50,700
Yes.

267
00:19:52,033 --> 00:19:53,967
Hey, Jin Ho, that hurts.

268
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:58,100
You know who your competition
for Joey is, right?

269
00:19:59,267 --> 00:20:01,033
Competition?
Who?

270
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,567
Andrew?

271
00:20:02,700 --> 00:20:04,100
Come on.

272
00:20:04,233 --> 00:20:06,533
You know I don't compete with,
you know...

273
00:20:07,700 --> 00:20:09,333
- Okay.
- I don't compete!

274
00:20:09,467 --> 00:20:11,167
Okay.
So cool.

275
00:20:11,900 --> 00:20:13,367
So I guess you don't need this.

276
00:20:13,500 --> 00:20:15,700
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

277
00:20:15,833 --> 00:20:17,267
I kind of like that too.

278
00:20:17,833 --> 00:20:19,300
But what's your point?

279
00:20:20,267 --> 00:20:22,633
Have you seen Andrew's style?

280
00:20:23,867 --> 00:20:25,700
And have you seen yours?

281
00:20:27,067 --> 00:20:28,533
Wow, now you're insulting me.

282
00:20:28,667 --> 00:20:30,867
You know what? This style?

283
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,000
We call dibs on this back
in San Isidro.

284
00:20:33,133 --> 00:20:34,500
Don't you know that?

285
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,333
Bro...

286
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:40,667
Let's just try this, okay?

287
00:20:41,267 --> 00:20:42,833
Just follow my advice.

288
00:20:42,967 --> 00:20:44,267
I'm telling you...

289
00:20:44,400 --> 00:20:47,233
Joey will stop noticing
Andrew...

290
00:20:47,367 --> 00:20:50,167
and start noticing you.

291
00:20:50,933 --> 00:20:52,433
You sound pretty confident.

292
00:20:52,967 --> 00:20:54,200
Are you sure?

293
00:20:55,100 --> 00:20:58,067
Just like you, I don't compete.

294
00:20:58,200 --> 00:20:59,900
I prepare.

295
00:21:15,833 --> 00:21:17,133
Thank you.

296
00:21:19,100 --> 00:21:21,933
Why did you leave the eatery?

297
00:21:22,367 --> 00:21:24,300
Didn't I tell you to stay there?

298
00:21:24,433 --> 00:21:26,000
Where did you even go?

299
00:21:28,033 --> 00:21:30,067
I thought I saw Dad,

300
00:21:30,600 --> 00:21:31,133
so I followed him.

301
00:21:31,267 --> 00:21:32,667
But then, he disappeared.

302
00:21:36,533 --> 00:21:38,067
I don't get it.

303
00:21:38,633 --> 00:21:40,067
You're looking for your dad,

304
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:42,233
that's why you're here
in Valmora?

305
00:21:43,133 --> 00:21:48,800
Actually, Joey's dad
is a police officer.

306
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:51,267
Major Miguel Delgado.

307
00:21:51,867 --> 00:21:54,600
He was chasing a lead
here in Valmora,

308
00:21:54,733 --> 00:21:56,967
but he hadn't even gotten
far from Bolagos

309
00:21:57,433 --> 00:21:59,167
when his car exploded.

310
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:04,867
But I believe
Dad is still alive.

311
00:22:05,367 --> 00:22:06,933
I really have
a strong feeling he is.

312
00:22:07,067 --> 00:22:09,267
He's here to find Berdugo.

313
00:22:10,233 --> 00:22:11,833
Berdugo?

314
00:22:29,267 --> 00:22:30,167
So your theory is that

315
00:22:30,300 --> 00:22:32,200
Berdugo will replace
Godfather as the supplier

316
00:22:32,333 --> 00:22:33,367
here in Valmora.

317
00:22:33,500 --> 00:22:34,933
Delilah, I'm all set
for my treat.

318
00:22:35,067 --> 00:22:36,533
- And the sample?
- It's ready too.

319
00:22:36,667 --> 00:22:37,967
You won't be disappointed.

320
00:22:38,100 --> 00:22:39,567
I'm looking forward
to putting a face

321
00:22:39,700 --> 00:22:41,600
to the mysterious Berdugo.

322
00:22:41,733 --> 00:22:43,400
I really want to land

323
00:22:43,533 --> 00:22:45,400
this exposé.

324
00:22:45,533 --> 00:22:46,967
Or maybe you're doing this
for...

325
00:22:47,100 --> 00:22:49,200
For helping my friend.

326
00:22:49,367 --> 00:22:50,500
That's all it is.

327
00:22:50,633 --> 00:22:52,833
So you can honestly say you
don't have feelings for her?

328
00:22:52,967 --> 00:22:55,167
One, two...
You can do it!

329
00:22:55,300 --> 00:22:56,167
Do I really need all this

330
00:22:56,300 --> 00:22:57,467
just for her to notice me?

331
00:22:57,600 --> 00:22:58,867
You're a good guy, Peter.

332
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,200
You'll be good for Joey.

333
00:23:00,333 --> 00:23:02,567
She just needs to see you
in a different light.

334
00:23:02,700 --> 00:23:05,333
And please, instead of calling
me “oppa,” call me “hyung.”

335
00:23:05,467 --> 00:23:06,567
No, no, I'm not used to it.

336
00:23:06,700 --> 00:23:07,867
- Hyung! Hyung!
- Oppa!

337
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:09,300
Once I find Dad,

338
00:23:09,433 --> 00:23:11,033
I won't be a burden
to you anymore.

339
00:23:11,167 --> 00:23:13,133
- Hello?
<i> - Joey, my child.</i>
